{n:7,where:"Marquee Mile, Harborlight fundraiser",seed:"Before the stadium is public, a volunteer asks you to sign the \"New Levee\" petition.",rev:"Act 3 hearing: Bennett reads your name out as a supporter, with Gus in the room.",into:"Gus's trust; a scene where you explain.",p:2,r:3,who:["bennett","gus"]},
{n:8,where:"Marquee Mile, the Aurelian",seed:"The tourist you taught at the table is a travel writer.",rev:"Opening night: her piece names you and the crowd is bigger.",into:"Opening-night flavour; first-week takings.",p:2,r:5,who:[]},
{n:9,where:"Silvershore, the Obsidian",seed:"A society columnist asks how much Vivian lost tonight. Tell her (she pays) or keep quiet.",rev:"Act 5: Vivian knows who talked. Quiet makes the land cheaper; talking sends her toward Tae.",into:"Land price; Vivian's standing.",p:3,r:5,who:["vivian"]},
{n:10,where:"The Levee, the RailYard",seed:"Sign up for the players' card with a face scan, or pay cash and keep your head down.",rev:"Act 4: Wren quotes your losses and where you've been. A spotless player gets a threat against Gus or Jalen instead.",into:"Wren's deal; Ed trusts you more if you never scanned in.",p:1,r:4,who:["wren","ed","jalen"]},
{n:11,where:"The Bridges, Long Bridge",seed:"Crossing before dawn despite Dot's warning (hoodlums, no organization), you see Ray's car with the lights off. Note the other car's plate or drive on.",rev:"Act 4 loose ends: the plate is the filing lawyer's. Ray handed him Gus's sale contract and took a secret finder's fee behind Wren's back, after swearing he never met the man.",into:"Leverage on Ray.",p:2,r:4,who:["dot","ray"]},
{n:12,where:"Anywhere",seed:"A man sells a \"lucky spaceman\" bobblehead. Buy it or laugh.",rev:"Gus laughs at it, and that's all.",into:"Nothing, on purpose.",p:2,r:0,who:["gus"]},
{n:13,where:"Marquee Mile, the Aurelian",seed:"A Revaris rep pitches Tae a state-of-the-art AI camera system, better than the chain's own and priced well below its worth, and corporate pushes him to take it. Warn him (through Felix/Nora or Stella) or say nothing. He installs it either way. The pitch comes before the Flare's sale goes through (A2.2); if you can't reach the Aurelian in time, he installs it with no chance to warn him.",rev:"Act 5: if you warned him, Tae remembers you were right and goes easier in the land fight, or pays a fair price if he buys the name. If Revaris was exposed as Umbra in act 4, the Aurelian rips the cameras out and takes a reputation hit.",into:"Tae's standing; the land contest; outcome 5 price.",p:2,r:5,who:["tae","felix","stella","wren","vivian"]}
