const OUT=[
{n:1,name:"The lakefront Starflare with Gus",act:5,final:true,leads:"The name won back for Gus, Vivian's land won, a big bankroll, Gus trusts you. Gus signs the name over to you and comes to opening night as a guest to cut the ribbon; he never owns or hosts the new Starflare.",back:"Final: ends the main story.",after:"Light owner mode; the tower (~$2M) and rooftop launch pad (~$1.5M) as goals.",who:["gus","rosa","pete","jalen","vivian","miles"]},
{n:2,name:"The Starflare without Gus",act:5,final:true,leads:"As 1, but you use the leverage to take the name for yourself (ruthless; for example buying it from Wren at A4.3 at a price plus a favor) or Gus has turned on you.",back:"Final: ends the main story.",after:"Light owner mode; Gus never appears on the floor and some regulars stay cool.",who:["gus","bennett","rosa","vivian"]},
{n:3,name:"The Starflare floats",act:5,final:false,leads:"The name won back, a mid-sized bankroll, an old boat (seed 5) and the dockworkers on your side; the land falls through.",back:"Win the land later and move ashore.",after:"The boat is a venue you run lightly, after a short license hearing.",who:["gus","rosa"]},
{n:4,name:"The people's Starflare",act:4,final:false,leads:"The name won back while you're short of $250k (the regulars' offer at A4.10), or the land falls through in act 5; the regulars pool small shares and reopen on a shoestring, Gus hosting (no union stake). Players who never get rich settle here.",back:"A stepping stone: it earns you income in light owner mode; at $250k act 5 opens, the regulars come with you as crew and their shares are paid back on opening night.",after:"Co-op nights at the union hall, after a short license hearing; light owner mode shared with the regulars.",who:["gus","rosa","kasia","juan","jalen"]},
{n:5,name:"Tae's restaurant",act:4,final:false,leads:"You side with Tae and Stella; Tae buys the name from the Stadium District. The District (really Revaris and Wren) never sells the name to Gus's side, because the name in your hands is a threat; Tae is a neutral buyer (a chain wanting a restaurant brand), so they take his money. Once Tae holds it, it's ordinary private property (audit 4.7). Gus greets guests; the band photo and the old rocket sign hang inside (only the band photo if the Flare burned), and if you got Tae his father's drum kit at {A3.3}, it sits on a riser under the photo.",back:"Buy the name back from Tae at a premium once you hold the land (fair price after the house band reunion, or if you warned him about the cameras, {S13}).",after:"A hangout inside the Aurelian with Gus at the door.",who:["tae","gus","stella","bennett"]},
{n:6,name:"Gus lets go",act:4,final:false,leads:"You help Gus quit and bring back Dot and Stella; nobody funds a reopening. It doesn't need the name: Gus stops fighting for it, and it stays wherever it is while the Field timer runs.",back:"Win the name back later, and a sober Gus asks you to reopen.",after:"Visits with sober Gus, Dot and Stella at the Slack Water picnic table.",who:["gus","dot","stella"]},
{n:7,name:"The name stays with Starflare Field",act:4,final:false,leads:"The default if Starflare Field opens before anyone wins the name back; the Stadium District keeps it.",back:"Win the name back later by leverage.",after:"Games at Starflare Field under the old rocket sign, restored over the gate.",who:["bennett","gus"]},
{n:8,name:"Mob takeover",act:4,final:false,leads:"You hand Wren Raffy's drive at A4.5, or deep debt to Ray and a crooked lean. Safe at last, she pulls the name out of the District through Revaris and keeps you on as hers. Her Starflare is the Revaris showcase: a licensed, polished casino wired with her cameras, with Umbra money underneath.",back:"Expose Wren later to take the name (leads to 2).",after:"Wren's Starflare, the Revaris showcase, with you in it.",who:["wren","ray","raffy","gus"]},
{n:9,name:"Burned down",act:3,final:false,leads:"A setback you play through, not an ending. Only after the last night (A3.3): you fight the demolition dirty with high heat, or cross Umbra, and Umbra torches the empty Flare as a message before demolition. The old rocket sign, still on the shell, is lost for good.",back:"Play on. The name stays with the Stadium District, the Field is built on the burned site on its normal schedule (the timer doesn't change), and Jalen and Vivian won't back you until a season passes with no Umbra trouble.",after:"No epilogue of its own.",who:["gus","jalen","vivian"]},
{n:10,name:"The sellout",act:4,final:false,leads:"Betray Gus for a payout: bring him back to Wren's table and hand her his markers (act 4), or help Tae get Vivian's land (act 5). Gus, Dot and the regulars turn cold.",back:"Leverage can still take the name (leads to 2), or a long climb on generous and reliable wins Gus back (the only road to 1).",after:"Comped life on the Mile (Tae) or Umbra favors (Wren).",who:["wren","tae","vivian","gus"]}
];
