const MYST=[
{id:"M1",name:"The torn patch",kind:"Backstory",truth:"Rosa's torn patch is from the Starflare. Gus, drunk, lost the staff payroll at her table, so she dealt him back to even. Cameras caught it and she took the fall without saying why. The commission only ever saw the overhead dealer camera: Rosa's hands and the chip flow, no faces. Gus kept the only wide-angle tape, which shows him in the seat (audit 3.7). The commission's penalty ordered a modern camera system Gus couldn't afford, which led to Wren's camera deal.",
clues:["Rosa won't step inside the Flare (broke)","Pete goes quiet at her name (Flare regular)","The surveillance tape: in Gus's office before the fall, in Bennett's hands after it (Miles/Audrey saw it taken)","Her commission file via Vivian's lawyer (rich)"],
solve:"Gus admits it; Pete and Gus testify and Rosa gets her license back. First proof that Gus gambles.",who:["rosa","gus","pete","bennett","vivian","miles"]},
{id:"M2",name:"Who bought the Flare",kind:"Main story",truth:"Who is Revaris really, and why won't Gus say its name? The sale is public: Revaris Technologies, a camera company, bought the Flare. Nobody outside knows it is Umbra's front; Gus signed knowing it was the mob and, ashamed, tells everyone \"a friend of Ray's\" bought it. Umbra then put the land into the Levee Stadium District, which makes Revaris (Umbra's company) the biggest investor on paper; and Bennett pushed the deal through for campaign money and a hidden cut, which Wren pays herself through Revaris, so her own books are the proof and she owns him. False leads: Stella (meeting Tae, but only asking him who's really behind Revaris) and Tae (would have bought it openly).",
clues:["Stella and Tae at the Aurelian (rich)","The buyer is public (Revaris Technologies, the camera company) and Gus still says \"a friend of Ray's\" (free)","Proof Revaris is Umbra's front: the opened ledger on Raffy's drive (Ray's name and Cinder Room men beside Revaris ID numbers; a locked drive is only a hint), or working off your debt to Ray puts you in the room when he calls the company \"us\" (broke)","Mitch recognizes the filing lawyer from Bennett's old deals (broke)","Felix/Nora show you Revaris's lawyer meeting Bennett at the Aurelian (romance)"],
solve:"Opens act 4: you know Umbra bought the Flare and that Wren owns Bennett. Clearing Stella brings her and Gus closer.",who:["bennett","wren","ray","stella","tae","mitch","raffy","felix"]},
{id:"M3",name:"The Prairie Queen skim",kind:"Backstory",truth:"Ray makes Kiran (who borrowed from him to pay off a loan he co-signed for his wife's brother) and other indebted dealers skim the cheap tables to cover his bad loans. The skim steals from the house (palmed chips on color-ups, a short-counted drop box), never from players, so play at his table is always fair. He thinks it's behind Wren's back, but her cameras are on the Queen: she knows and lets him dig his own hole.",
clues:["Kiran's tell and Rosa flagging a table (broke)","Ray's new car he can't afford","Ed's file on Ray"],
solve:"Kiran gets out. Tell Wren through her lawyer (Ray learns she knew and is humbled; costs heat), tell Ed (informant path), or keep it as leverage on Ray.",who:["ray","kiran","wren","ed","rosa"]},
{id:"M4",name:"Room 9 and Gus's box",kind:"Backstory, leads to the main story",truth:"The quiet guest in room 9 is Richard, Bennett's father, whose house went to Flare markers. Bennett traced Gus's camera deal to Umbra and forced Gus to wipe out Richard's remaining debt in exchange for his silence. Ashamed, Gus gave Richard the key to a safety deposit box rented in Richard's name (it opens only with his signature) holding the original signed camera contract and Gus's own recording of Bennett's demand (a recorder in his desk; Bennett picked the office because it is off the floor cameras), the only copy. Bennett pays the room weekly; Richard thinks Gus does. Umbra can't use the key without Richard's signature, so it watches the door to see if he goes to the bank.",
clues:["Dot sees a driver drop an envelope every week (broke)","A photo of Richard on Bennett's desk (rich)","War with Richard at the picnic table: the house he lost, Gus \"takes care of\" his room (false lead), the game he taught his son","A dark sedan in the Slack Water lot before dawn, watching room 9's door"],
solve:"Once Richard trusts you, Umbra men who followed you come to room 9 with his old Flare markers (Revaris owns the books) and demand payment or the key; Gus's condition is met and you open the box together. Richard decides: shame Bennett into amending his stadium ordinance to return the name to Gus, give Bennett the box and reconcile (they play War; out of gratitude Bennett files the same amendment), burn it, or hand it to Ed (Ed's case, but Gus's deal comes out). Any public use exposes Gus too.",who:["richard","bennett","dot","gus","ed"]}
];

